{# The alert every `hx-confirm` asks through, in place of the browser's
   confirm(): that one is titled with the site's address, drawn by the
   browser, and worded in the browser's language, and nothing else on a
   page gave it away as a web page so plainly.

   htmx fires `htmx:confirm` before a confirmed request; cancelling that
   event hands the decision to us, and `issueRequest` / `dropRequest` give
   it back. The action button is named for what it does -- the control's
   own words, "Delete" or "Remove member" -- rather than OK, and Cancel is
   the one that has focus, so Return never destroys anything by itself.
   A control with no words of its own, or whose yes destroys nothing, says
   so: `data-confirm-action` names the button, and `data-confirm-tone="plain"`
   makes it the primary one rather than the red one, without the warning.

   The script for both is frontend/site/alerts.ts. #}
<div id="ds-confirm" class="ds-modal ds-alert" style="display: none;" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-describedby="ds-confirm-message">
  <div class="ds-modal-panel ds-alert-panel">
    <p id="ds-confirm-message" class="ds-alert-message"></p>
    <div class="ds-alert-actions">
      <button type="button" class="ds-button" data-confirm-cancel>{{ ftl_get_message("cancel") }}</button>
      <button type="button" class="ds-button ds-button-danger" data-confirm-ok>{{ ftl_get_message("delete") }}</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script>if (window.oeeeChrome) window.oeeeChrome.confirmDialog();</script>
{# The same alert with nothing to decide: something the page has to say, and
   OK. `dsAlert(message)` stands in for the browser's alert(), which the
   Android app draws as the web view's own box, titled "oeee.cafe says", and
   the Apple and Windows apps do not draw at all. The site calls neither
   alert() nor confirm() (frontend/shared/siteDialog.ts). #}
<div id="ds-alert" class="ds-modal ds-alert" style="display: none;" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-describedby="ds-alert-message">
  <div class="ds-modal-panel ds-alert-panel">
    <p id="ds-alert-message" class="ds-alert-message"></p>
    <div class="ds-alert-actions">
      <button type="button" class="ds-button ds-button-primary" data-alert-ok>{{ ftl_get_message("ok") }}</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script>if (window.oeeeChrome) window.oeeeChrome.alertDialog();</script>
